  <title>COPY MEMO Command</title>
  <keywords>
    <keyword>Commands</keyword>
    <keyword>Memo fields</keyword>
    <keyword>COPY MEMO command</keyword>
  </keywords>
  <body>
    <header>
      <para styleclass="Heading1">COPY MEMO Command</para>
    </header>
    <para styleclass="Normal"><snippet src="__FoxProOnly" inline="false"/></para>
    <para styleclass="Normal"><snippet src="__CommandInclude" inline="false"/></para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">Purpose</para>
    <para styleclass="Normal">Copies the contents of a memo field of the current record to a file.</para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">Syntax</para>
    <para styleclass="Code with box">COPY MEMO &lt;MemoField&gt; TO &lt;FileName&gt; [ADDITIVE] [AS &lt;nCodePage&gt;]</para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">Arguments</para>
    <para styleclass="List">&lt;MemoField&gt;<tab />The name of the memo field in the current work area.</para>
    <para styleclass="List">TO &lt;FileName&gt;<tab />The name of the file that receives the contents of the memo field.</para>
    <para styleclass="List">ADDITIVE<tab />Appends the contents to the end of the file when it already exists. Without this clause an existing file is overwritten.</para>
    <para styleclass="List">AS &lt;nCodePage&gt;<tab />The code page of the text that is written to the file. When this clause is omitted, the text is written without conversion.</para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">Examples</para>
    <para styleclass="Code Example">USE Customers<br/>
COPY MEMO Notes TO CustomerNotes.txt<br/>
COPY MEMO Notes TO AllNotes.txt ADDITIVE</para>
    <para styleclass="Body Text"><snippet src="__IncludeLibRT" inline="false"/></para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">See Also</para>
    <para styleclass="Normal"><link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="command_REPLACE_FoxPro">REPLACE (FoxPro)</link>, <link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="html\M_XSharp_RT_Functions_DbCopyMemo.htm" domain="XSharpRef.chm">DbCopyMemo()</link></para>
  </body>
